  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable the telemetry-related service (DiagTrack)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagTrackService_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure the "Connected User Experiences and Telemetry" (DiagTrack) service and the connection for the Unified Telemetry Client Outbound Traffic. Disabling the service may prevent you from getting XBOX achievements and affect Feedback Hub. The Windows Insider Program will also be unavailable.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Configure the level of diagnostic data collected by Windows</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Required diagnostic data is the minimum that Windows needs to stay secure, up to date, and working as expected. Optional diagnostic data adds details about how you use apps and features. With required data only, the Windows Insider Program is unavailable. On the Enterprise and Education editions, diagnostic data is turned off instead.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Optional diagnostic data</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_DiagnosticDataLevel_Title_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Required diagnostic data only</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable Windows Error Reporting</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_ErrorReporting_Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The error reporting feature enables users to notify Microsoft of application faults, kernel faults, unresponsive applications, and other application-specific problems. Microsoft can use the error reporting feature to provide customers with troubleshooting information, solutions, or updates for their specific problems.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="UIModel_FeedbackFrequency_Title" xml:space="preserve">
